.TH DREAM-LOG 1 "2026-08-12" "dream-log 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dream-log \- log and manage dream entries in a Notion database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dream-log
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dream-log
(the
.B dream_logger.sh
script) is a Bash utility that stores dream journal entries in a Notion
database via the Notion API. Each entry has a title, a description, and a
status.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B query
List all entries in the database, printing each entry's id, title, and
status.
.TP
.BR log " " \fItitle\fR " " \fImsg\fR
Add a new dream entry with the given title and description.
.TP
.BR update " " \fIpage_id\fR " " \fImsg\fR " " \fIstatus\fR
Update an existing entry's description and status.
.I status
must be one of
.BR New ", " Reviewed ", or " Done .
.TP
.BR amend " " \fImsg\fR " " \fIstatus\fR
Update the description and status of the most recently created entry,
without needing its page id.
.TP
.BR get-id " " \fItitle\fR
Print the page id for the entry matching
.IR title .
.TP
.BR del " " \fIpage_id\fR
Delete (archive) the entry with the given page id.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B dream-log
reads its configuration from environment variables, falling back to a
.I .env
file (see
.B FILES
below) for any that are unset.
.TP
.B NOTION_TOKEN
Notion integration token used to authenticate API requests.
.TP
.B DATABASE_ID
The 32-character hex id of the target Notion database.
.TP
.B API_URL
Base URL for the Notion API, e.g.
.IR https://api.notion.com/v1 .
.TP
.B NOTION_VERSION
Notion API version header, e.g.
.IR 2022-06-28 .
.TP
.B DREAM_LOG_DIR
Directory to look for a
.I .env
file in when the variables above are not already set. Defaults to
.IR $HOME/dream-log .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $DREAM_LOG_DIR/.env
Shell-sourced file defining
.BR NOTION_TOKEN ", " DATABASE_ID ", " API_URL ", and " NOTION_VERSION .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
if required dependencies or configuration are missing, if a Notion API
request fails, or if invalid arguments are given.
.SH EXAMPLES
List all dream entries:
.RS
.EX
dream-log query
.EE
.RE
Log a new dream:
.RS
.EX
dream-log log 'Flying over mountains' 'I was soaring above snowy peaks at dusk.'
.EE
.RE
Update an entry by id:
.RS
.EX
dream-log update 36ec4fd1-da0d-813a-97c3-d550fce7d7e6 'Vivid colours.' Done
.EE
.RE
Amend the most recent entry without looking up its id:
.RS
.EX
dream-log amend 'Vivid colours, felt very real.' Done
.EE
.RE
Look up an id by title, then delete it:
.RS
.EX
dream-log del $(dream-log get-id 'Flying over mountains')
.EE
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.BR curl (1),
.BR jq (1),
and a Notion integration token for a database shared with that integration.
.SH SEE ALSO
Notion API documentation: https://developers.notion.com
.SH AUTHOR
duutabib
